[medium] Matching model IDs with substring `includes` risks false positives (e.g., user-defined model names that happen to contain these tokens). If the set of model IDs is known, an exact comparison — or a lookup set / anchored regex matching the expected patterns — would be safer. It would also help to normalize case in one place, since model IDs aren't always consistently cased.

```suggestion
		const normalizedModelId = modelId.toLowerCase()
		const isDeepseekReasoner =
			normalizedModelId === "deepseek-reasoner" || normalizedModelId === "deepseek-r1"
```
